              _a_s_s_u_m_e___d_e_f_a_u_l_t___c_o_l_o_r_s_(_-_1_,_-_1_)_;

       These are _n_c_u_r_s_e_s extensions.  For other curses implementations,  color
       number -1 does not mean anything, just as for _n_c_u_r_s_e_s before a success‐
       ful call of uussee__ddeeffaauulltt__ccoolloorrss or aassssuummee__ddeeffaauulltt__ccoolloorrss.

       Other curses implementations do not  allow  an  application  to  modify
       color  pair  0.  They assume that the background is COLOR_BLACK, but do
       not ensure that the color pair 0 is painted to  match  the  assumption.
       If  your  application  does  not  use  either uussee__ddeeffaauulltt__ccoolloorrss or aass‐‐
       ssuummee__ddeeffaauulltt__ccoolloorrss _n_c_u_r_s_e_s will paint a white foreground  (text)  with
       black background for color pair 0.

